  "contract_changes": [
    "Copywriter output is a typed ordered sections list derived from PresentationPacket.section_order.",
    "Comparison and image comparison permit only a model summary; backend owns comparison rows.",
    "Single-product suitability and product knowledge bind evidence to their visible answer or judgement section.",
    "Image identity, clarification, and error are deterministic and do not call the copywriter.",
    "Allowed facts grant permission only; model coverage is checked against required dimensions visible in model-owned sections.",
    "The deterministic fallback uses the same typed section contract and prioritizes required dimensions.",
    "Every writer section now has an explicit content source: summaries, closings, and general knowledge are constraints-only; product, answer, and judgement sections may use approved facts.",
    "Constraints-only sections reject product fact IDs even where their historic evidence location was visible-product scope.",
    "Approved facts preserve exact child dimension IDs from ConceptSlotData through narrative atom aggregation, fallback selection, validation, prompt payload, and gate coverage.",
    "The adapter and compiler reject the retired universal summary/product/closing draft.",
    "Compact tags are backend-only 2-4 character fact indexes and are outside model coverage.",
    "The real copywriter runner persists the current result and stops after the first hard failure."
